course: dictionary
lesson: 1721
title: Words for water and pipes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cistern is a tank that holds water. Context tells you which kind. In a house, «When you flush, a valve opens and water from the cistern rushes into the bowl» means the cistern is the tank that feeds the toilet bowl with water.
explain: Read the words around the word. A float that «rises as the cistern refills» shows that the cistern gets full again after it empties, so refills means fills up again.
explain: Some cisterns are in the loft or under the ground, and in dry places long ago they stored rainwater. The context tells you which meaning the writer means, so read on before you decide.
fact: A cistern is a tank that stores water.
fact: The cistern in a toilet fills up after you flush.
fact: A float rises as the cistern fills, and it shuts off the water when the tank is full.
fact: Most toilet flushes use several litres of water.
fact: In old times and dry places, people built large underground cisterns to collect rainwater, as in ancient cities such as Istanbul.
exercise: «When you flush, a valve opens and water from the cistern rushes into the bowl.» What is the cistern? | *The tank that holds water for flushing | The pipe that carries waste away | The handle you press to flush
exercise: «Old cities in dry lands built a huge underground cistern to save rainwater.» What does cistern mean here? | *A large tank for storing water | A deep well for oil | A kind of cloud | A small room for washing
exercise: «A float rises as the cistern refills.» What does refills mean? | Breaks down | *Fills up again | Gets cleaned | Empties completely
test: «The cistern refills and shuts off the water when it is full.» What shuts off the water when the cistern is full? | The bowl | The pipe outside | *The float, which rises as the water rises | The handle
test: Where might a cold-water cistern be found in a house? | *In the loft, or under the ground | In the garden shed | In the bedroom wardrobe | Inside the fridge
exam: A plumber says «the cistern is refilling». What is refilling? | The floor under the sink | The toilet seat | The pipe to the garden | *The tank that holds the water
